{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792398083,"nonce":"Pb4JvGTo3FND9v3t0Psp+Ez5JGk=","title":"hxml parser misses standard Haxe options","message":"`compiler/src/hxml.rs` (`HxmlConfig::from_string`) handles `-cp`, `--class-path`, `-main`, `-lib`, `-D`, `-resource`, `-debug`, `-v`, `--output` and the rayzor flags. It treats every traditional target as \"ignored\". Missing, compared with haxe 4.3/5:\n- long forms `--main`, `--library`, `--define`, `--resource`, `--debug`, and the short `-p`;\n- `-lib name:version` and resolving libraries to class paths through haxelib (including each library's own `extraParams.hxml`);\n- including another hxml by naming it on a line (`other.hxml`);\n- `--next` and `--each` sections;\n- quoted and space-containing arguments, several flags on one line, `#` comments after flags;\n- target flags (`--js out.js`, `--cpp dir`, `--hl`, `--jvm`, `--interp`, `--neko`, `--python`, `--lua`, `--php`, `--cs`, `--java`, `--swf`) recorded as the target with its implied defines instead of being dropped;\n- `--macro`, `--dce`, `--no-inline`, `--no-opt`, `-w`, `--connect`/`--wait` (parsed and reported, even if not honoured).\n\nUnknown flags should be reported with their line, not silently skipped.","files":null}]}